          "grounding_supports": [
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 311,
                "end_index": 488,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The CENTCOM Intelligence Scandal (2015)\nIn U.S. military and political circles, \"Intelgate\" (short for *Intelligence Gate*) refers to the **CENTCOM analyst controversy of 2015**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 491,
                "end_index": 677,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **The Scandal:** In mid-2015, over 50 military and intelligence analysts working for the U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM) filed a formal complaint with the Pentagon\u2019s Inspector General"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3,
                1,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 679,
                "end_index": 911,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "They blew the whistle on senior military leaders and intelligence officials, accusing them of systematically altering, softening, or suppressing intelligence reports regarding the U.S.-led fight against ISIS (ISIL) in Iraq and Syria"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 914,
                "end_index": 1188,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **The Core Issue:** The analysts alleged that their reports were manipulated to present a falsely optimistic and politically convenient picture of the war\u2014making it look like the coalition was winning, while suppressing realistic, downbeat assessments of ISIS's strength"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1190,
                "end_index": 1376,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **The Outcome:** A 2016 Congressional task force agreed that CENTCOM\u2019s senior leaders consistently distorted intelligence to paint a rosier picture than facts on the ground warranted"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1378,
                "end_index": 1644,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "However, a 2017 Department of Defense Inspector General report ultimately cleared senior officials of *intentional* or malicious falsification, attributing the issues instead to a toxic \"command climate,\" severe communication breakdowns, and poor editorial standards"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1659,
                "end_index": 1871,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Intel Corporation\u2019s Spectre, Meltdown, and Stock Sale Scandal (2018)\nIn the corporate and technology world, \"Intelgate\" was widely used in early 2018 to describe a massive crisis involving **Intel Corporation**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1874,
                "end_index": 2136,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **The Scandal:** In January 2018, security researchers publicly disclosed **Spectre and Meltdown**\u2014two catastrophic, hardware-level vulnerabilities that affected nearly every modern computer processor on Earth, with Intel CPUs being the most severely exposed"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2139,
                "end_index": 2346,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **The Controversy:** The scandal deepened into \"Intelgate\" when it was revealed that Intel\u2019s then-CEO, Brian Krzanich, had sold off approximately $24 million worth of Intel stock and options in late 2017"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                8,
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2348,
                "end_index": 2509,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "He executed this sale *after* Intel had been privately warned of the flaws by Google\u2019s security researchers, but *before* the public or investors were informed"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2511,
                "end_index": 2647,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This sparked massive public outrage, congressional inquiries, and class-action lawsuits accusing Intel\u2019s leadership of insider trading"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11,
                12
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2662,
                "end_index": 2899,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Intel's 13th and 14th Generation CPU Instability Crisis (2024)\nMore recently, tech hardware enthusiasts and consumer watchdogs have used \"Intelgate\" to refer to a devastating product-quality scandal involving Intel\u2019s desktop processors"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                13
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2902,
                "end_index": 3173,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **The Scandal:** Throughout late 2023 and 2024, game developers and PC enthusiasts noticed that high-end 13th and 14th generation \"Raptor Lake\" desktop processors (such as the Core i9-13900K and i9-14900K) were experiencing severe, irreversible crashing and instability"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3806,
                "end_index": 3909,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This fiasco is widely referred to in modern PC hardware circles as \"Intelgate\" or the \"degradation bug\""
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14,
                15
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3924,
                "end_index": 4199,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The \"Russiagate\" Political Counter-Narrative (2017\u20132018)\nDuring the investigation into potential Russian interference in the 2016 U.S. presidential election (often called \"Russiagate\"), some political commentators and critics of the probe used \"Intelgate\" as a counter-term"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14,
                15
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 4266,
                "end_index": 4484,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Cohen writing in *The Nation*) argued that the real scandal was not Russian collusion, but rather that elements within the U.S. intelligence community (the FBI, CIA, and NSA) had overstepped their constitutional bounds"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14,
                16
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 4486,
                "end_index": 4686,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "They alleged that intelligence agencies had fabricated or weaponized unverified information (such as the Steele Dossier) to spy on and actively run an operation against the Trump presidential campaign"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
          ],
